    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **261 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented email uniqueness for owner creation, respond\u00ading 409 when the lower-cased email is already used by another owner. Following the OfficeFloor function-injection pattern in this repo, I mirrored the existing telephone-unique feature:\n\n**New files**\n- `EnsureOwnerEmailUnique.java` \u2014 pipeline step: reads the normalized (already lower-cased) `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, and throws `DuplicateEmailException` if `ownerRepository.findByEmail(...)` returns any existing owner. Email is optional, so a null email short-circuits.\n- `DuplicateEmailException.java` \u2014 checked exception (`extends Exception`).\n- `DuplicateEmailExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 escalation handler responding `409 CONFLICT` via `ProblemDetail`.\n- `.../escalation/...DuplicateEmailException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted an `ensureEmailUnique` step (with `govern: [ transaction ]`) after `ensureTelephoneUnique`, so it runs after email normalization/lower-casing and before `build`/`save` (duplicate \u2192 409, no persisted row).\n- `OwnerRepository` interface + all three implementations (`SpringDataOwnerRepository`, `JpaOwnerRepositoryImpl`, `JdbcOwnerRepositoryImpl`) \u2014 added `findByEmail`, using a `LOWER(email) = LOWER(:email)` comparison so matching is case-insensitive regardless of how existing rows were stored.\n\nThe pre-existing `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` (create with an email, then create again with the same email \u2192 expect 409) now passes, and all 261 tests remain green.",
